                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This visual novel is definitive proof that visual novels may be the greatest medium for engrossing yourself in a fantasy world and long term storytelling. The combination of music, sound effects, sprite movement, cgs, and even mech gameplay have turned what would have been a masterpiece of a novel series into a living, breathing world you can spend 100 hours in of pure enjoyment and suspense for the greatest payoff of all time. Never in my life have i read, watched, or heard of anything with such a masterful implementation of amnesia/flashbacks, the mystery isn't solved in the first route and just like life, answers to your questions are answered with more questions until the final question is answered only in death. You are handed bits and pieces of the full story in flashbacks during routes, and then you are handed massive chunks of important storytelling during the climax of each route. Each heroine is an extremely compelling character, they interact with the mc in a believable fashion and are not simply set pieces for romance. Because it is such a long story it has ample time to invest in the development of side characters as well as the main cast, It makes me profoundly sad that most people will never experience what it is like to dedicate nearly a hundred hours to a story like Baldr Sky because of pre-conceived notions about visual novels and not wanting to \"read a game\"; the investment itself is most enjoyable while being able to dedicate so much time to building payoffs that cannot exist without so much time spent with the characters and in the world. This game is a 9.9/10 only held back by it's horrendously outdated engine and being locked into Fullscreen (maybe was a good thing since I could truly focus).",
